Similarly, to run read_diag_rad.exe, the namelist file namelist.rad is needed. It contains
the same parameters as namelist.conv. Using the same case from section 5.2, copy
diag_amsua_n18_ges.2011032212 to directory ./util/Analysis_Utilities/read_diag
(executable sits in this directory) and then change the namelist.rad to:
&iosetup
infilename='./diag_amsua_n18_ges.2011032212',
outfilename='./results_amsua_n18_ges',
/
Running the executable creates the text file results_amsua_n18_ges specified by the
namelist in the directory read_diag_rad.exe runs.
For the conventional observations, the data is stored in two arrays: rdiagbuf and cdiagbuf.
Their contents are listed as follows:
Cdiagbuf    = station id
rdiagbuf(1) = observation type
rdiagbuf(2) = observation subtype
rdiagbuf(3) = observation latitude (degrees)
rdiagbuf(4) = observation longitude (degrees)
rdiagbuf(5) = station elevation (meters)
rdiagbuf(6) = observation pressure (hPa)
rdiagbuf(7) = observation height (meters)
rdiagbuf(8) = observation time (hours relative to analysis time)
rdiagbuf(9) = input prepbufr qc or event mark
rdiagbuf(10)= setup qc or event mark (currently qtflg only)
rdiagbuf(11)= read_prepbufr data usage flag
rdiagbuf(12)= analysis usage flag (1=use, -1=not used)
rdiagbuf(13)= nonlinear qc relative weight
rdiagbuf(14)= prepbufr inverse obs error (K**-1)
rdiagbuf(15)= read_prepbufr inverse obs error (K**-1)
rdiagbuf(16)= final inverse observation error (K**-1)
rdiagbuf(17)= temperature observation (K)
rdiagbuf(18)= obs-ges used in analysis (K)
rdiagbuf(19)= obs-ges without bias correction (K)



For wind observations, the content after index 16 is:

rdiagbuf(17) = u wind component observation (m/s)
rdiagbuf(18) = u obs-ges used in analysis (m/s)
rdiagbuf(19) = u obs-ges w/o bias correction (m/s)
rdiagbuf(20) = v wind component observation (m/s)
rdiagbuf(21) = v obs-ges used in analysis (m/s)
rdiagbuf(22) = v obs-ges w/o bias correction (m/s)

!

The read_diag_conv.exe reads these arrays and outputs important information in the text
file results_conv_anl specified by the user in the &iosetup namelist. Example:


      Station   Obs   Obs    Obs    Obs     Obs    Obs    iuse    obs     O-F    oberror (always occupies last column)
      ID        Type  Time   Lat    Lon     Press  Hght         value   (ddiff)
ps @  21997   : 180   0.00  42.65  190.98  1013.20     10   1   1013.2   -0.35     2.0
t  @  PADK    : 187  -0.07  51.88  183.35   993.34    200   1    276.0    0.33     2.0
uv @  RD01709C: 242  -1.48  40.50  189.00   886.30  10000   1     14.04   3.12   -11.80  -0.24  2.0


Note that for the uv field the last 4 variables are: uob, uob-uges, vob, vob-ges

For q the output from this program converts from kg/kg to g/kg!


